 "traditions": [],
 "notes": "Old 'Pot still whisky' (k119) became Irish single pot still whiskey; Redbreast, Spot and Powers models turned into archetype versions. Midleton Very Rare is a blend per Wikipedia, so it sits under Irish whiskey (Barry Crockett Legacy kept as its single pot still version); Kilbeggan Rye moved to Irish whiskey m (rye mash, not single pot still). Old Crown Royal Fine De Luxe became a version. Non-Scotch models handed over from the Scotch shelf (05_00) added as versions (Amrut Fusion, Kavalan Solist Vinho Barrique, Yoichi 10, Sullivans Cove TD0112, Jameson Triple Triple, MVR 2026, Tullamore 12) or flat models (Teeling x4 deduplicated to 3, The Donn, Titanic, Fercullen, Ichiro's Malt & Grain, Sakurao, Starward, Callington Mill, English Distillery, Thy, KI ONE, Kwun Cheung, Waterloo); American ones (St George Baller, Stranahan's, Longleaf, Frey Ranch) belong on the American whiskey shelf. Left out: Redbreast 27 'YO' duplicate SKU names, Sullivans Cove versions (no wiki page; only award fact used), Starward/Lark/Milk & Honey archetypes (single-line mentions only), Nordic distilleries other than Mackmyra (Stauning, Kyrö, Box not on any retrieved page), Lot 40 versions/awards (no retrieved page beyond Canadian whisky), Suntory brand facts from knowledge."
}